<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n26256" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">διαφῠή</span></b> , ἡ, (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">διαφύω</span>) <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>natural break, joint, suture,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὰ ὀστᾶ . . διαφυὰς ἔχει χωρὶς ἀπ᾽
					ἀλλήλων</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pl.
					<u>Phd.</u>
					98c
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Philostr.
				<u>VA</u>
				4.28
			</span></i>; <i>distinction,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Plt.</u>
				259d
			</span></i>; <i>dissepiment,</i> as in chestnuts, <i><span class="en">
				X.
				<u>An.</u>
				5.4.29
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				<u>Cic.</u>
				1
			</span></i>; <i>joint</i> in reeds or grasses, <i><span class="en">
				Longus
				1.10
			</span></i>; <i>divisions</i> between the teeth, <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				<u>Pyrrh.</u>
				3
			</span></i>; <i>cleft</i> in rocks, <i><span class="en">
				D.S.
				5.22
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>stratum</i> or <i>vein</i> of earth, stone, metal, <i><span class="en">
				Thphr.
				<u>Lap.</u>
				63
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δ. καὶ φλέβες</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					D.S.
					3.12
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>III.</b>
			<i>string-basket,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				PRyl.
				97.7
			</span></i>
			<span class="entity">(ii B.C.)</span>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
